    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d205">

                <pb facs="0253" n="137" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg137"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/942.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Extract.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-06-14">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 14, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Minister of Finance has served written demand on the bankers to answer by
                    June 15 whether or not they will advance 19,000,000 taels more during June;
                    otherwise he will get the money elsewhere. He knows that the bankers cannot
                    answer definitely within the time be has fixed, as they are dependent on the
                    result of the Paris meeting. The ultimatum suggests interference from outside at
                    this end. It is <pb facs="0254" n="138" xml:id="pg138"/> reported that Tong has
                    been conferring with the Russians. Possibly Russia prefers to have the Chinese
                    break with the groups here and thereby relieve her of the onus of forcing a
                    rupture in Paris.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Calhoun.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
